    "created_at": "2014-09-25T15:28:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2014-09-25T15:28:41Z",
    "body": "Linux systems will trust that keyboard, I suspect that OS X and Windows will too.\n\nWe don't really have a well-defined notion of _intent_ when dealing with Bluetooth devices. If I pair a device through the UI, do I intend to use that device as a keyboard, or with an app, or both? If I only intend to use it through an app, how do I subsequently use it with additional apps, or as a system device?\n\nIt's not a technology problem, adding a service whitelist to the device database is trivial. It's a UX one.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
